      remote flap of port1.0.3 / 1.0.4 / 1.0.2 from the stack ... PASS  (3 x down/up each, seen
                                            by the x230; links back a-full a-1000)
      LLDP neighbours on 1.0.2/1.0.3/1.0.4 . PASS  (same three before and after each step)
CAVEAT:  "supported speed" = 1000 Mb/s full duplex (autonegotiated), the speed every live x230
         link runs at on this bench; no other speed was flapped. port1.0.5's partner is a host NIC
         (tb470 eth3), so it was flapped locally only. port1.0.1 had no link (its AR4050S partner
         port is shut down) and was not flapped.

